---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const POLICY_VERSION = "2026-07-17";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use — Ozzyl Recipes"
  description="Terms governing Ozzyl Recipes accounts, content, and platform use."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container legal-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Version {POLICY_VERSION}</p>
      <h1 class="section-title">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="section-copy">These terms describe the account and contributor foundation currently implemented for Ozzyl Recipes. They must be reviewed by the business before public registration is enabled.</p>

      <h2>Accounts</h2>
      <p>Users must provide accurate account information, protect their credentials, and use the service lawfully. Email verification is required before a full authenticated session or trusted write action is allowed.</p>

      <h2>Recipes and contributions</h2>
      <p>Contributors must submit content they have the right to share. Content may be reviewed, edited, rejected, unpublished, or removed for quality, safety, legal, or community reasons.</p>

      <h2>Cooking information</h2>
      <p>Recipes, timing, nutrition, and measurement conversions are informational. Users remain responsible for food safety, allergies, dietary suitability, appliance use, and professional advice where needed.</p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>Users must not abuse accounts, automate harmful traffic, bypass security controls, upload malicious content, impersonate others, or interfere with the platform or its users.</p>

      <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
      <p>Features may change, pause, or be removed. Account and content access may be restricted when necessary to protect users, comply with law, or maintain platform integrity.</p>

      <h2>Before public launch</h2>
      <p>This draft must be replaced or approved by qualified legal counsel for the operating company, jurisdiction, refund model, advertising model, contributor licensing, and dispute terms before production registration is enabled.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
